    {
      "id": "session:2026-10-20-84137a84",
      "type": "Session",
      "label": "Council, step 0, and closing kg",
      "description": "Goal: Decide whether to revive kg after the scrapy result.\nInstructions: An unofficial council: nothing goes to the repo until there is a good idea.\nDiscoveries: Part of the loss was kg's own implementation (re-validating the store on every read, importing matplotlib, --depth 0 rejected). With kg fast and next to search, the gate failed on time. The lean control shows the prompt line explains the saving where kg was not used.\nAccomplished: Council run; #67 opened with a numeric gate; fast reads and companion (#68), merged by the user; lean control; option 1 chosen; report and README (#69, #70); v0.3 issues and the milestones closed; project marked concluded in memory.\nNext steps: None for v0.3. If reopened: the string-edges idea, better as a contribution to an existing tool. The harness can measure other tools.\nRelevant files: docs/report.md, docs/benchmark.md, docs/roadmap.md, bench/README.md, README.md",
      "attrs": {
        "date": "2026-10-20",
        "commit": "e066c56",
        "transcript": "84137a84",
        "order": 11
      },
      "provenance": {
