    {
      "id": "experiment:council",
      "type": "Experiment",
      "label": "An unofficial council reviewed the state of kg",
      "description": "What: Set up after Karpathy's llm-council: subagents as experts researched similar tools and what kg could borrow or add, then cross-reviewed and synthesised. Explicitly unofficial; its good idea became #67.\nLearned: It suggested taking string edges to existing tools with users (code-review-graph, codebase-memory-mcp, or libraries such as grimp or import-linter) as a plugin, PR or small library, and was about 50% sure nothing does it yet, after a short search.",
